<title>FRANCE: PRESS DIGEST - Algeria - Jan 25.</title>
<headline>PRESS DIGEST - Algeria - Jan 25.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>These are the leading stories in the Algerian press on Saturday. Reuters has not verified these stories and does not vouch for their accuracy.</p>
<p>EL MOUDJAHID</p>
<p>- President Liamine Zeroual underlines the government firmness to fight &quot;terrorism&quot;.</p>
<p>EL WATAN</p>
<p>- Zeroual throws political accusations across the board but fails to outline any new political prospect to end the crisis.</p>
<p>- Massacres continue in Blida: 29 people killed.</p>
<p>AL KHABAR</p>
<p>- Zeroual denounces the &quot;terrorism&quot;.</p>
<p>- Violence continues: Twenty-six people assassinated.</p>
<p>LE MATIN</p>
<p>- More than 50 people killed in a bloody weekend.</p>
<p>ALAM ASSIASSI</p>
<p>- The Transitional National Council begins debates on party and election laws.</p>
</text>
